 "about": "Beech and silver fir on the wet north side; Scots pine, downy and Portuguese oak, black pine and box on the drier south side; oak, ash, chestnut and birch in the low valleys, holm oak on hot limestone; upright mountain pine with alpenrose, juniper and bilberry at the treeline; purging broom in the east, gorse, heather and bracken in the west, hedgehog broom on southern limestone, eskia fescue on the high slopes, white asphodel in the pastures; cattle, large sheep flocks, horses, goats and Pyrenean chamois. Hawthorn stands in for the apple orchards.",
